---
import '../../details/zetta-joule.css'
import frames from '../../details/zetta-frames.json'
const asset = '/details/zetta-joule/'
// These are public Jumi utilities, shared verbatim with the inspection panel.
const entrance = 'animate-opacity-[0:0|100:1] animate-translate-[0:0_36px|100:0_0] animation-duration-[1400ms] animation-timing-function-ease-out animation-fill-mode-both'
const reveal = 'data-[entered=true]:animate-opacity-[0:0|100:1] data-[entered=true]:animate-clip-path-[0:inset(0_100%_0_0)|100:inset(0_0%_0_0)] animation-duration-[1000ms] animation-timing-function-ease-out animation-fill-mode-both'
const progress = 'animate-opacity-[0:0|100:1]/frames animation-timeline-[--reactor]/frames animation-range-[contain_0%_contain_100%]/frames animation-timing-function-linear/frames animation-fill-mode-both/frames'
const benefit = 'animate-opacity-[0:0|100:1]/reveal animation-timeline-[--reactor]/reveal animation-range-[contain_30%_contain_60%]/reveal animation-timing-function-linear/reveal animation-fill-mode-both/reveal'
const media = 'animate-clip-path-[0:inset(0_15%_0_35%)|100:inset(0_0%_0_0%)] animation-timeline-[--mission] animation-range-[entry_70%_contain_70%] animation-timing-function-linear animation-fill-mode-both'
const charts = ['Cities & Infrastructure','Materials & Manufacturing','Fuels & Upstream','H₂ Hydrogen']
const chartFiles=['cities','materials','fuels','hydrogen']
const notes=[
 ['Hero entrance',entrance,'Document time. Opacity and translation settle together. The tiled curtain is an independent scale-X phrase with small per-tile delays. Exact load timing is an approximation. The whole scale property is used because the current scale-x phrase drops its keyframe values; see the conformance audit.'],
 ['Section entrance',reveal,'The reference text continues revealing after scrolling stops. IntersectionObserver only sets entered=true; Jumi owns the ensuing document-time opacity and clipping. The simplified block wipe does not reproduce the original character-by-character staggering.'],
 ['Mission media',media,'The clip opens around the original footage. The video renders its own recorded motion; Jumi controls only the surrounding reveal.'],
 ['Reactor sequence',progress,'Motion driver: Jumi / CSS scroll timeline. Progress choreography: Jumi. Frame rendering: a small canvas media bridge reading this element’s animated opacity as a normalized scalar. Discrete media decoding is outside Jumi’s CSS property model.'],
 ['Reactor annotations',benefit,'A separate named reveal shares the reactor driver, placed later in its contain range. CSS position: sticky pins the composition.'],
]
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>ZettaJoule | Jumi motion study</title><meta name="description" content="An independent ZettaJoule motion study built with public Jumi utilities and native CSS."/><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg"/></head><body>
<div class="curtain" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from({length:64},(_,i)=><i class="animate-scale-[0:1_1|100:0_1] animation-duration-[850ms] animation-delay-[var(--tile-delay)] animation-timing-function-ease-in-out animation-fill-mode-both" style={`--tile-delay:${100+(i%16)*22+Math.floor(i/16)*70}ms`}/>)}</div>
<main>
<section class="hero" id="hero">
<header class="reference-nav"><a class="brand" href="https://zetta-joule.com/" aria-label="Original ZettaJoule site"><i class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"/>ZettaJoule</a><nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Original website">{[['Company','about-us'],['Technology','technology'],['Solutions','solutions'],['Our Edge','our-edge'],['Our Team','team'],['Investors','investors-private'],['News','news']].map(([label,path])=><a href={`https://zetta-joule.com/${path}`}>{label}</a>)}</nav><a class="contact" href="https://zetta-joule.com/contact">Get in Touch</a><details class="mobile-nav"><summary aria-label="Navigation">☰</summary><nav><a href="#mission">Mission</a><a href="#technology">Technology</a><a href="#reactor">Reactor</a><a href="#heat">Heat capabilities</a><a href="https://zetta-joule.com/">Original website ↗</a></nav></details></header>
<h1 class="hero-title"><span data-motion class={`${entrance} animation-delay-[450ms]`}>Powering</span><span data-motion class={`world ${entrance} animation-delay-[650ms]`}><span>the</span><span>World</span></span></h1>
<img data-motion class={`hero-reactor ${entrance} animation-delay-[200ms]`} src={`${asset}hero.webp`} alt="Cutaway of the ZettaJoule reactor" fetchpriority="high"/>
<p data-motion class={`hero-note ${entrance} animation-delay-[850ms]`}>Clean Heat and Electricity<br/>to Power a World of<br/>Industrial Applications</p>
</section>
<section id="mission" class="section mission-intro"><div class="split"><h2 class="eyebrow">The Name Reflects our Mission</h2><div class="copy" data-motion data-entered="false" class:list={[reveal]}><p>Projections by the U.S. Department of Energy show that annual global energy demand by the year 2050 will reach one billion times one trillion (zetta) units of energy (joules).</p><a class="link-button" href="https://zetta-joule.com/about-us"><b>↳</b><span>Discover Our Story</span></a></div></div></section>
<p class="tablet-mission-copy">Our name, ZettaJoule, reflects our commitment to being part of the solution for meeting this tremendous need by providing clean, reliable heat and power.</p>
<section class="mission-story"><div class="mission-sticky" data-motion data-scroll class:list={[media]}><video class="mission-video" data-mission-video muted loop playsinline preload="none" poster={`${asset}poster.webp`} aria-label="ZettaJoule industrial energy film"><source data-src={`${asset}mission.mp4`} type="video/mp4"/></video><img class="city" src={`${asset}city.webp`} alt="A city at night" loading="lazy"/><p class="mission-copy" data-motion data-entered="false" class:list={[reveal]}>Our name, ZettaJoule, reflects our commitment to being part of the solution for meeting this tremendous need by providing clean, reliable heat and power.</p><div class="definition"><div>ZettaJoule<br/>\ ˈze-tə-ˌjül \</div><p>One zettajoule equals 10²¹ joules, or one billion trillion joules.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="technology" class="section technology"><div class="split"><h2 data-motion data-entered="false" class={reveal}>Modernizing<br/>Proven Technology</h2><div class="copy" data-motion data-entered="false" class:list={[reveal]}><p>Established reactor technology, modernized for industrial heat up to 950 °C.</p><a class="link-button" href="https://zetta-joule.com/technology"><b>↳</b><span>Explore Our Technology</span></a></div></div><figure class="building"><img data-motion data-scroll class="animate-scale-[0:1.12|100:1] animation-timeline-[--building] animation-range-[entry_0%_exit_100%] animation-timing-function-linear animation-fill-mode-both" src={`${asset}building.webp`} alt="ZettaJoule’s proposed energy campus beside a river" loading="lazy"/><figcaption data-motion data-entered="false" class:list={[reveal]}>● Design Meets Resilience<p>A contemporary energy campus designed to sit thoughtfully within its surroundings.</p></figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="reactor" class="reactor-section"><div class="split"><h2 class="eyebrow">Intelligent Systems</h2><p class="copy" data-motion data-entered="false" class:list={[reveal]}>Digital systems support a new generation of industrial energy.</p></div><div class="reactor-scroll"><div class="reactor-stage"><span data-frame-progress data-motion data-scroll class={`frame-progress ${progress}`} aria-hidden="true"></span><canvas data-reactor data-frames={JSON.stringify(frames)} width="1360" height="765" aria-label="Scroll-driven exploded reactor assembly"></canvas><img class="reactor-still" src={`${asset}reactor-mobile.webp`} alt="Reactor assembly" loading="lazy"/><span class="reactor-label">ZJ REACTOR</span><dl class="specs"><dt>REACTOR TYPE</dt><dd>HTGR</dd><dt>GENERATING CAPACITY</dt><dd>30 MWTH</dd><dt>HEAT OUTPUT</dt><dd>UP TO 950 °C</dd></dl><div class="reactor-benefits">{[['Heat','High-temperature process heat for industry.'],['Heat & Power','Combined heat and electricity.'],['Hydrogen','Heat for efficient hydrogen production.'],['Electricity','Reliable power, around the clock.']].map(([title,copy])=><article data-motion data-scroll class={benefit}><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div></div></div></section>
<section id="heat" class="section heat"><div class="split"><h2 data-motion data-entered="false" class={reveal}>Unmatched<br/>Heat Capabilities</h2><p class="copy" data-motion data-entered="false" class:list={[reveal]}>High-temperature heat opens up a wider range of industrial applications.</p></div><div class="chart-tabs" aria-label="Heat applications">{charts.map((title,i)=><button data-chart={i} aria-pressed={i===0}>{title}</button>)}</div><div class="chart"><img src={`${asset}chart.webp`} alt="Operating temperature comparison of reactor technologies" loading="lazy"/>{chartFiles.map((file,i)=><img data-chart-panel={i} class="chart-overlay" hidden={i!==0} src={`${asset}${file}.webp`} alt={`${charts[i]} temperature requirements`} loading="lazy"/>)}</div></section>
</main>
<footer class="study-footer"><h2>ZettaJoule / Motion study</h2><p>An independent Jumi recreation of <a href="https://zetta-joule.com/">ZettaJoule’s website</a>. No affiliation or endorsement. Original imagery and film belong to their respective owners.</p><p>This first study covers the hero, mission, technology campus, reactor assembly and heat comparison. Typography uses system fonts; some supporting copy is condensed. The sequence renderer is a disclosed media adapter, not a second animation system.</p><p class="no-scroll">Your browser does not support CSS scroll timelines. This study preserves readable static content instead.</p><a href="/">Built with Jumi ↗</a> · <a href={`${asset}provenance.json`}>Asset provenance</a></footer>
<aside class="study-bar" aria-label="Jumi study controls"><a href="/">Jumi ↗</a><span class="study-name">ZettaJoule · Motion study</span><a href="https://zetta-joule.com/">Original ↗</a><button data-inspect>How it moves</button></aside>
<dialog class="inspect"><header><h2>How it moves</h2><button data-close>Close</button></header><p>Independent recreation · public Jumi syntax + native CSS.</p>{notes.map(([title,classes,note])=><details><summary>{title}</summary><pre>{classes}</pre><p>{note}</p></details>)}<details><summary>Honest boundaries</summary><p>The original desktop reactor is rendered imagery. Jumi supplies an animated 0-1 scalar; a media bridge selects and paints a frame. No scroll listener, JavaScript easing, or Jumi internals are involved.</p><p>Mobile uses the source site’s static reactor. Reduced motion disables entrances and footage while keeping content visible. Native CSS owns layout, clipping containers, sticky positioning and responsive rules.</p></details></dialog>
<script>import '../../details/zetta-joule'</script>
</body></html>
